396	// --- CLI: the thin I/O shell the vendored scheduler run workflow invokes ---------------
397	// Reads the work-item list, plans, applies. All GitHub access is the Action's
398	// GITHUB_TOKEN. Dormancy is the first gate, before any read — a project that has
399	// said it is out of the recurring work should not pay for the list that proves it.
400	
401	// Every WORK ITEM, state=all, via the ISSUES list API — never the search index
402	// (S6/F11: search is eventually consistent, and a family list that misses a
403	// just-created item mints a duplicate standing item). Bounded by the scheduled
404	// families' need for closed history: closed items are only interesting back to the
405	// widest period, so the listing stops once it is past that.
406	//
407	// MEMBERSHIP IS `isQueueItem`, the shared predicate, and not the title prefix
408	// (#1497). An adopted marked issue IS an item under the one-issue model
409	// (docs/PRINCIPLES.md) and keeps the person's own title forever, so a prefix test drops exactly
410	// that class — and job 2 is the ONLY site that releases a blocked item, so an
411	// ad-hoc item born blocked on a `Not-before:` sat sleeping past its instant with
412	// nothing left to wake it (#1267, #1349, #1351, #1396). The executor and the
413	// janitor already read the queue through this predicate; this list was the one that
414	// did not.
415	export async function listWorkItems(gh, repo, { since = null } = {}) {
